AWS 2-Tier Architecture with Terraform

📌 Overview

Built a 2-tier AWS architecture using Terraform:

Public EC2 – application/web tier
Private RDS MySQL – database tier
Secrets Manager – secure DB credentials
IAM Role + Instance Profile – EC2 access to the secret
Security Groups – control EC2 → RDS access

🏗️ Architecture::

                    Internet
                       │
                  HTTP / SSH
                       │
                       ▼
              ┌─────────────────┐
              │   Public EC2    │
              │  10.0.1.0/24    │
              │   WebServer SG  │
              └────────┬────────┘
                       │
                VPC Local Route
                  TCP 3306
                       │
                       ▼
              ┌─────────────────┐
              │  Private RDS    │
              │   MySQL 8.0     │
              │    RDS SG       │
              └─────────────────┘
                       ▲
                       │
              ┌────────┴────────┐
              │ Secrets Manager │
              └────────▲────────┘
                       │
                    IAM Role
                       │
                      EC2

🔐 Security :

RDS is not publicly accessible.
RDS 3306 allows traffic only from the EC2 Security Group.
RDS master password is managed by RDS + Secrets Manager.
EC2 retrieves the secret using its IAM Role.
No AWS access keys are stored on EC2.

🧪 Connectivity Tests :

EC2 → RDS
nc -vz logindb.cpwmk4e8u62p.ap-south-1.rds.amazonaws.com 3306
Connection ... 3306 port [tcp/mysql] succeeded!

✅ Network connectivity confirmed.

MySQL Authentication
mysql -h logindb.cpwmk4e8u62p.ap-south-1.rds.amazonaws.com -u admin -p
Welcome to the MySQL monitor.
Server version: 8.0.46
mysql>

✅ Database authentication confirmed.

EC2 → Secrets Manager
aws secretsmanager get-secret-value \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --secret-id "$SECRET_ARN"

✅ Secret successfully retrieved using the EC2 IAM role.

Automated Connection
EC2
 │
 ├── IAM Role
 │      ↓
 │  Secrets Manager
 │      ↓
 │  DB credentials
 │
 └──────────────→ Private RDS
                    MySQL : 3306

✅ End-to-end connectivity verified.

📚 Key Lessons :

Security Groups can reference other Security Groups.
EC2 → RDS uses the VPC local route; NAT Gateway is not required.
Instance Profile = attaches the role to EC2.
RDS-managed passwords avoid hardcoding DB credentials in Terraform.

🎯 Result

Successfully deployed and tested a Terraform-based AWS 2-tier architecture with private RDS connectivity, IAM-based secret retrieval, and verified MySQL access.
